# Security

## Planes

Tag every worker/service with plane: `research` | `validation` | `execution`.

- Separate credentials, networks, and object-store prefixes per plane
- Research MUST NOT read validation holdout credentials or execution trading secrets
- Execution has no live capital keys in initial phase; paper broker only when enabled

## Code execution

- Agent-generated and strategy code runs in sandbox: no outbound network unless explicitly allowlisted for data workers (not strategy sandboxes)
- CPU/memory/wall-clock limits enforced
- Strategy runtime: no wall-clock-based signals; event time injected

## Audit & change control

- Append-only audit for FSM transitions, tool calls, secret access denials
- Kill-switch capability for execution plane
- Rollbacks for config/methodology version pins

## Least privilege

- Tool gateways enforce role allowlists from RoleContract
- Agents cannot self-elevate
- Egress for Intelligence Agent via allowlist; record URL + content hash

## Forbidden shortcuts

- Shared `.env` across planes
- Disabling sandbox “for debugging” in committed configs
- Logging secrets or raw exchange keys
